; git clone -q --filter=blob:none \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" sw2 2>&1|tail -1; cd sw2; git log --oneline|head -2; sed -n '/^## 5/,/^## 6/p' Outline.md | head -30; grep -n -i 'venue-repo' Outline.md | …", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian; rm -rf sw2; git clone -q --filter=blob:none \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" sw2 2>&1|tail -1; cd sw2; git log --oneline|head -2; sed -n '/^## 5/,/^## 6/p' Outline.md | head -30; grep -n -i 'venue-repo' Outline.md | head"]], "output": "```console\n0113098 Outline rev. 13: §1 sentences 4-5 per review #8; ladder diagnostics and rank sensitivity\nfcd0f14 Outline rev. 12: OLB training-side rule result in C4\n## 5. Figures and tables (main text; presentation decides how they are drawn)\nVenue (`venue-repo`#2): NeurIPS 2026 main track, **9 content pages including figures and tables** (references, appendix, checklist excluded), 5.5 in text width. Venue's final answer: from 21 accepted NeurIPS evaluation/benchmark papers, median 6 figures+tables, **recommended 6, at most 7** (4 figures + 2 tables); this plan is 4 + 3 = 7, the ceiling. Allocation:\n\n| # | Says | Claim | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Fig. 1** | Error vs k on held-out groups, common-target-set score (§2b): S6+P5, random-k (mean + spread over C/T splits and draws), best-baseline pipeline, mean-offset baseline, the floor, and (if defensible) the predicted curve from T1; raw points and standardised units; k and k/N; k*(ε) marked. A lower panel (or inset) shows the paired difference design − random with group-bootstrap CI and the ±δ / +Δ bands, so the verdict is visible | C2, C3, C4 | full 5.5 in width; carries the old Fig. 4 |\n| **Fig. 2** | Matrix structure: the spectrum with the noise reference and the three rank estimates (coverage/missingness pattern goes to the appendix) | C1 | half width |\n| **Fig. 3** | Theory vs measurement: synthetic (known truth), predicted vs measured with the estimation term vs M; real-data residual = misfit | C4 | one panel per regime: separated factors, decaying spectrum, real |\n| **Fig. 4** | Scope map: headline quantity vs each condition (extrapolation, missing rate, M, transform, granularity, ladder with the real matrix placed by the §3-C6 rule) | C6 | small multiples; same y-axis where comparable; the old Fig. 5 |\n| **Table 1** | Coverage-filter table and final shape, held-out group counts per split | G1/G4 | mandatory; may be compressed |\n| **Table 2** | Primary contrast at k ∈ {1,2,3,5,8,12,20} with CIs and verdicts; the predicted vs empirical k*(ε) at ε = δ, 2δ with CIs | C3, C4 | merges the old Table 3 |\n| **Table 3** | Pipeline comparison: inference rules P0–P6 × {random-k, S6} at 3–4 k values, best-of-column marked | C3 | from review #3 |\n| App. | S×P full grid; coverage heat map; per-task-type and per-benchmark error; sensitivity (imputation, rank estimator, transform, restarts); T3 unit test; T4 simulation; adaptive vs batch (C5, main text only if there is a gain and space); Open LLM/HELM oracle checks; conditions-and-cost table if not in the main text; checklist; reproduction notes and search log | | |\n\n**As built (paper-repo `dev`, rev. 11):** main text holds Fig. 1, Fig. 3, Table 2 and Table 3; Fig. 2 (structure), Fig. 4 (scope map) and Table 1 are in the appendix — within the cut order below and accepted. The room this frees (4 of the ≤ 7 main-text figures+tables) is where the OLB block goes (C7): a small table of the OLB G/S curve, k*, gain and floor misfit rows, or a second panel in Fig. 1 if presentation can show it; the Fig. 4 role (scope conditions) is carried in the main text by the one paragraph and the appendix figure.\nIf the text does not fit, cut in this order (first first): Table 3 merges into Table 2 (the pipeline comparison becomes extra rows at fewer k values), Table 1 is compressed, Fig. 4 becomes a table row set, Fig. 2 becomes a half-width panel of Fig. 3. Fig. 1 and Table 2 stay; the pipeline comparison itself stays in the main text in some form. The main text also holds a Discussion-and-limits section (not only the appendix), the significance reporting and a compute statement; licences (MTEB results CC0-1.0; the Open LLM/LiveBench datasets declare none, recorded by analysis), code/data access and LLM-use go to the checklist. A negative branch (C3-B) must be a firm quantified statement with its equivalence test: the venue judges it by a higher significance bar.\n\n## 6. What each neighbour is asked, and what comes back to me\n86:Venue (`venue-repo`#\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "d32397fa-5d89-5f6b-b86b-6f2d63544375", "at": 1795738637.0439396, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 68917, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "0d1a0915c2a8bed1239a805f29d84ee0", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "419c10df-d6ff-5e72-8ab1-dd6e34828a39", "at": 1795738637.0463538, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 68918, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "0d1a0915c2a8bed1239a805f29d84ee0", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "6e830e8d-f12b-535c-87fb-b47c4ad29ea7", "at": 1795738637.049046, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 68919, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "0d1a0915c2a8bed1239a805f29d84ee0", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "869ae275-95e3-5503-8d0d-d84f0e9cf271", "at": 1795738637.0999417, "clo